WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
- This is what I love about you.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.533
Cause I actually,

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:04.300
in the beginning of my
career turned down deals

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.420
because it literally
was like selling my soul

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.600
if I signed the dotted
line, and I was like, look,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.650
I'm a waitress and I don't have anything,

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.590
but you're not gonna hold
that over my head and take

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.220
everything from me.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.053
I was like, and nobody understood that.

00:00:15.053 --> 00:00:17.680
They always thought
that I was being a diva.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.243
And like, you should just
take what you're given.

00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:22.280
And I heard that you
were actually offered,

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.160
you turned down a million
dollar signing bonus

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.670
during that time. Right
before Piece Of You, right?

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.920
- Yeah, I was homeless.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.130
I ended up living in my
car because I wouldn't

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.160
have sex with the boss.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.180
And so I was living in my car,

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.350
and then my car got stolen
and I started gigging

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.510
to try and just get by.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.180
And I ended up getting discovered
accidentally after a year.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.810
And there's a bidding war
over me. It was crazy.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.880
And I was offered a million
dollar signing bonus,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.316
but I realized it was a loan. And I had to

00:00:45.316 --> 00:00:47.720
give that money back through record sales.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.320
And I wanted to make an honest record.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.680
Like I made myself a promise
at the beginning of my career

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.510
that I would be a happy human
before I would be a musician.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.343
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:00:55.343 --> 00:00:57.320
- And that I would choose art over fame.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.660
And that really helped me navigate.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.370
And it's why I made decisions like that,

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.930
and it saved my career, that
record failed for over a year.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.560
And they would have
dropped me unquestionably.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.260
And the fact that I
turned that money down,

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.580
and I also took the biggest
back-end anybody had gotten.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.270
So that once I started selling
records, I really made money.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:15.270
- Yeah. I mean and that's the thing I tell

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.030
even like the artists on The
Voice that I work with now,

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.680
cause I'm from a singing
competition and I talk to them,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.430
I'm like, look, I love
the, any door's a good door

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.000
as a singer, or artist, or writer.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.660
However, you are. Any door's, a good door,

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.120
but what you do once you get through it,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.120
and the character that you're,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.960
you've got to live with that decision,

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.230
like for the rest of your life.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.670
- Yeah! I think that's why
you're one of the only successful

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.840
artists to come out of
those singing shows,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.700
because if singing was all it took,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.760
there'd be a lot of famous
people from those shows.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.620
It takes a lot of character,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.520
a lot of grit, and work ethic,
and a lot of other things,

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.650
and not selling yourself
short, like as artists

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.880
we cannot want to be famous
more than we want to be

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.560
happy as humans, you know?

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.140
- Oh my gosh, you would make
an amazing coach on The Voice.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.260
I'm just saying, I would pick you.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.250
- Well, you know, I'm here.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.540
- I would pick you. I was
like, and I think, you know,

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:02.560
I literally, it's so funny.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.010
You took the words right out of my mouth.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.170
I say it all the time. Like, look,

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.790
the show is about many different voices.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.960
The main one obviously vocally
like impressing people,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.010
moving people, but it's
also your character.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.880
People watch the show, they see you,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.900
they see your personality,
they buy into all of it,

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.393
you know? And so it's so true.
I agree with you on that.

